# 06 Per-call resource limits: pcre2_set_match_limit(),
#    pcre2_set_depth_limit(), pcre2_set_heap_limit(), pcre2_set_offset_limit()
# https://www.pcre.org/current/doc/html/pcre2api.html
#
# Not exposed by PHP.
#
# What it is: every single match call can carry its own budgets via a
# match context. Computation steps (match limit), backtracking depth, heap
# bytes and how far into the subject a match may start (offset limit).
# PHP has exactly two of these, and only as process-wide INI settings
# (pcre.backtrack_limit and pcre.recursion_limit). The in-pattern
# (*LIMIT_MATCH/DEPTH/HEAP) verbs can only LOWER budgets. A heap-limit
# abort shows up in PHP as the generic "Internal error". The offset limit
# has no PHP equivalent at all, and neither do other context settings like
# max_pattern_length.
# pcre2test can also DISCOVER the minimum budgets a match needs
# (find_limits). Nothing in PHP can measure that.
#
# What it enables: a tight budget around untrusted input at the one call
# site that needs it, instead of one global knob. It also caps where in a
# large buffer a match may begin, and find_limits shows what a match
# actually costs.

# Expect: Minimum heap limit = 6
#         Minimum match limit = 2621440
#         Minimum depth limit = 43
#         No match
# Limit discovery: pcre2test binary-searches the budgets this exact match
# needs. 2.6 million steps just to fail on 20 characters... the numbers
# alone tell you the pattern is dangerous.
/(a+)+$/
    aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa!\=find_limits

# Expect: Failed: error -47: match limit exceeded
# The same runaway match under a per-call budget of 10 steps. It is cut
# off as a hard error, distinct from "No match".
/(a+)+$/
    aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa!\=match_limit=10

# Expect: No match
# Offset limit: the match may not START beyond offset 2, so the 'b' at
# offset 3 is out of reach. (Needs a pattern compiled with
# use_offset_limit.)
/b/use_offset_limit
    aaab\=offset_limit=2

# Expect: 0: b
# The same call with the limit raised past the match position.
/b/use_offset_limit
    aaab\=offset_limit=5
